# RNV publishing agent — optional per-machine overrides
#
# YOU PROBABLY DO NOT NEED THIS FILE.
#
# The chain resolves each path in this order:
#   1. the environment           - explicit, always wins
#   2. this file (.env)          - per-machine, gitignored, never committed
#   3. a sibling of this repo    - the normal case
#
# Rung 3 means that if the three repos are cloned next to each other, nothing
# here is required and a fresh machine works untouched:
#
#     <anywhere>/rnv-publishing-agent      <- this repo
#     <anywhere>/rnvizion.github.io        <- BLOG_REPO
#     <anywhere>/rnv-ask-the-corpus        <- CORPUS_REPO
#
# That holds in a Codespace (/workspaces), on a laptop (~/rnv), on a Desktop
# layout, or anywhere else. The absolute path differs per machine; the
# relationship does not, and the relationship is what gets derived.
#
# Set something below only when your layout does NOT fit that shape.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Check what actually resolves, and from which rung:
#
#     python tools/preflight.py --slug <your-post>
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Site checkout: the repo ROOT, the folder containing blog/.
# A relative value resolves against THIS repo, not your shell's directory, so
# ../my-site means the same thing from anywhere.
# Windows: use C:/Users/... form. Native Python cannot resolve /c/Users/...
# Quote any path containing spaces.
# BLOG_REPO="C:/Users/<you>/somewhere-else/rnvizion.github.io"

# Corpus checkout. Only stage 5 reads it, so a wrong value used to fail at the
# very end of an otherwise successful publish; it is now checked before the push.
# CORPUS_REPO="C:/Users/<you>/somewhere-else/rnv-ask-the-corpus"

# Live origin wait_for_live polls. No trailing slash.
# SITE_URL="https://rnvizion.dev"

# ONLY needed for agent.py, the conversational route. The tools, the demo, and
# the test suite all run without it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."
